{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134864-how-were-garou-able-to-hunt-down-other-feras-to-near-extinction","id":1134864,"title":"How were Garou able to hunt down other Feras to near extinction?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-28T10:23:32-07:00","id":1134864,"title":"How were Garou able to hunt down other Feras to near extinction?","content":"Are wolves stronger than a lot of the other were animals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T10:30:11-07:00","id":1134870,"title":"","content":"IIRC, it's the population difference. Tigers are in India and Asia, lions are in Africa, bears are wider spread but lower in population. Wolves, though. Dang, those fuzzy bastards seem to be almost everywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T12:02:11-07:00","id":1134890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134864-how-were-garou-able-to-hunt-down-other-feras-to-near-extinction?p=1134870#post1134870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC, it's the population difference. Tigers are in India and Asia, lions are in Africa, bears are wider spread but lower in population. Wolves, though. Dang, those fuzzy bastards seem to be almost everywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, tigers and lions tend to successfully exclude wolves from their territory.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also why is this in the general WoD when it's Werewolf-specific?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T13:55:05-07:00","id":1134933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134864-how-were-garou-able-to-hunt-down-other-feras-to-near-extinction#post1134864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are wolves stronger than a lot of the other were animals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Real wolves?<br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> Garou? Yes.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T14:08:24-07:00","id":1134944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134864-how-were-garou-able-to-hunt-down-other-feras-to-near-extinction?p=1134890#post1134890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, tigers and lions tend to successfully exclude wolves from their territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other other hand, one pride of lions can intimidate a pack of wolves fairly easily. One or two Simba intimidating a pack of Garou is another thing. I always understood the Bastet to be fairly solitary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 08-28-2017, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T16:54:55-07:00","id":1134994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134864-how-were-garou-able-to-hunt-down-other-feras-to-near-extinction?p=1134944#post1134944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other other hand, one pride of lions can intimidate a pack of wolves fairly easily. One or two Simba intimidating a pack of Garou is another thing. I always understood the Bastet to be fairly solitary.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Den Realm goes a long way toward helping you to make a holiday in hell for anyone trying to find you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T20:14:14-07:00","id":1135043,"title":"","content":"The idea that the Garou Beat the other breeds is a profoundly Eurocentric view. Look at Africa it sure looks like the garou were the losers there. Asia's even better for Fera thriving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T23:59:07-07:00","id":1135082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134864-how-were-garou-able-to-hunt-down-other-feras-to-near-extinction#post1134864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are wolves stronger than a lot of the other were animals?</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall Garou being in packs, while the other Fera tend towards being solitary, as one of the reasons why Garou had/have the edge over the other Fera war/combat-wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T02:09:20-07:00","id":1135102,"title":"","content":"If I recall right, the fact that the Simba of the Bastet and the Ajiba hang in prides instead of being solitary is the very reason the Garou never really gained a foothold in Africa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T03:18:37-07:00","id":1135381,"title":"","content":"Werewolves slaughtered other fera in Europe, Australia, and the Americas. I think the view of them as genocidal monsters is because the other fera never really committed invasive genocide. Sure, the other fera dominate Africa and east Asia, but those places never had a strong wolf presence to begin with. In other words, the other fera dominate in places where garou have almost no lupus kinfolk and never did. The garou moved into three continents that did have a strong fera presence at one point, and genocided them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T06:56:03-07:00","id":1135428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134864-how-were-garou-able-to-hunt-down-other-feras-to-near-extinction?p=1135381#post1135381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves slaughtered other fera in Europe, Australia, and the Americas. I think the view of them as genocidal monsters is because the other fera never really committed invasive genocide. Sure, the other fera dominate Africa and east Asia, but those places never had a strong wolf presence to begin with. In other words, the other fera dominate in places where garou have almost no lupus kinfolk and never did. The garou moved into three continents that did have a strong fera presence at one point, and genocided them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The golden jackal is also, now anyway, known as the African wolf, as it is a wolf rather than a jackal. Wolves were also known over Asia, though apparently the Red Talons in India pulled another Kuchu Ekunda, because they're found among the dholes, and dholes are about as removed from wolves as the African wild painted dog. They were there, but any counterattacks or counter-invasions are thus far still in the realm of being implied over explicit, and once you move east of India, you get into Beast Courts territory, and they had a different problem.<br /> <br /> The Ananasi did try to provoke the Garou, though, and used them and other Fera to this end. Not just to crack Ananasa's prison, either, since we have even Mokole recounting that they did something that was really dirty pool back in the day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T07:47:27-07:00","id":1135443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134864-how-were-garou-able-to-hunt-down-other-feras-to-near-extinction?p=1135082#post1135082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall Garou being in packs, while the other Fera tend towards being solitary, as one of the reasons why Garou had/have the edge over the other Fera war/combat-wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>The odd thing is that the three extinct Fera came from social animals and were known to live in large groups themselves. If anything the Garou seemed to unleash more devastation on the social Fera than they did on the solitary ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T15:16:46-07:00","id":1135620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134864-how-were-garou-able-to-hunt-down-other-feras-to-near-extinction?p=1135381#post1135381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves slaughtered other fera in Europe, Australia, and the Americas. I think the view of them as genocidal monsters is because the other fera never really committed invasive genocide. Sure, the other fera dominate Africa and east Asia, but those places never had a strong wolf presence to begin with. In other words, the other fera dominate in places where garou have almost no lupus kinfolk and never did. The garou moved into three continents that did have a strong fera presence at one point, and genocided them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's completely wrong? There have always been signficant wolf populations in SE Asia. China alone today has more Wolves than Europe. Japan used to have two seperate subspecies of wolf that was pushed into extinction in the early part of the 20th century(with some claims to survival among cryptozoologists), Mongolia has more wolves than the United states. Really the only country that Beats Asia ones for wolves is Canada.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T16:06:06-07:00","id":1135631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134864-how-were-garou-able-to-hunt-down-other-feras-to-near-extinction?p=1135443#post1135443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The odd thing is that the three extinct Fera came from social animals and were known to live in large groups themselves. If anything the Garou seemed to unleash more devastation on the social Fera than they did on the solitary ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, now it seems like the Garou shouldn't have even been able to wipe out the Grondr. They would have been fairly evenly matched to begin with, and then add on support of other Fera, and, well, now we're just getting into fiat territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T19:59:05-07:00","id":1135664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134864-how-were-garou-able-to-hunt-down-other-feras-to-near-extinction?p=1135631#post1135631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, now it seems like the Garou shouldn't have even been able to wipe out the Grondr. They would have been fairly evenly matched to begin with, and then add on support of other Fera, and, well, now we're just getting into fiat territory.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Grondir don't seem to have had the support of others? I definately head towards the SHattered Dream interpretation of the War of Rage as rather than &quot;garou vs everyone&quot; its a lot of conflicts back and forth The Grondir seem to have been less well liked broadly than the garou(Which is impressive) so while I don't imagine other Fera took an active hand they may have provided help that lead to the Grondir downfall.<br /> <br /> Now why Apsi aren't Spread out through all sorts of herd animals(buffalo etc) I don't know, I mean they litterally had special breeding powers and a mandate to help the Fera breed. Why wasn't a variant on every damned continent?<br /> <br /> I always thought the Camazotz should be like the Kitsune a fairly young breed that was endemic to central america and branching outward slowly. That would have made them easier to kill off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 08-30-2017, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T10:59:32-07:00","id":1135842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134864-how-were-garou-able-to-hunt-down-other-feras-to-near-extinction?p=1135664#post1135664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Grondir don't seem to have had the support of others? I definately head towards the SHattered Dream interpretation of the War of Rage as rather than &quot;garou vs everyone&quot; its a lot of conflicts back and forth The Grondir seem to have been less well liked broadly than the garou(Which is impressive) so while I don't imagine other Fera took an active hand they may have provided help that lead to the Grondir downfall.<br /> <br /> Now why Apsi aren't Spread out through all sorts of herd animals(buffalo etc) I don't know, I mean they litterally had special breeding powers and a mandate to help the Fera breed. Why wasn't a variant on every damned continent?<br /> <br /> I always thought the Camazotz should be like the Kitsune a fairly young breed that was endemic to central america and branching outward slowly. That would have made them easier to kill off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why weren't there Grondr in Asia? It's not like they lack for swine and swine-based monsters in folklore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T14:47:11-07:00","id":1135936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134864-how-were-garou-able-to-hunt-down-other-feras-to-near-extinction?p=1135842#post1135842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why weren't there Grondr in Asia? It's not like they lack for swine and swine-based monsters in folklore.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> IF we are talking folklore Foxes vs Rats. Grondr seem to have been more antisocial outside of breed than Garou. I am not sure I entirely buy it but even after committing countless atrocities against them the Mokole were more than willing to use their rights to let Garou breed outside wolves, the Grondr were never given this option. The Apis who should have that as part of their bailywick were never given this option.<br /> <br /> Camzotz do seem a good group all around though they have to use rituals to reproduce, they could be limited to new world bats, they are basically redundant with corax..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T14:21:27-07:00","id":1136368,"title":"","content":"As I've said before on related topics that I believe the &quot;War of Rage&quot; to be a problematic term because I don't think there technically was ever a &quot;war&quot;. Just like the term &quot;Hundred Years War&quot; is a concept invented by historians after the fact to categorize an era so is the War of Rage. It is a periodization. The different Changing Breeds killed each other before the &quot;War&quot;, during the &quot;War&quot;, and even after the &quot;War.&quot; Primitive peoples are almost always in a state of constant warfare with mortality rates far higher than those who live in civilized societies ruled by a strong state.<br /> <br /> It might just be that during the long period of the &quot;War of Rage&quot; that there were some particularly brutal conflicts that became conflated as a single conflict. This would explain why there are so many different legends on what started the &quot;war&quot;. Each of the Tribes and even each of the Changing Breeds have one (or more) stories of a big conflict, and from their perspective that became the &quot;origin&quot; of the &quot;war&quot;. That even the Mokole can't remember the &quot;origin&quot; is pretty good proof there was no &quot;origin&quot; because there never was such a war as the Changing Breeds now think there was.<br /> <br /> I also don't believe that the Garou are responsible for all the deaths either. The other Changing Breeds likely fought each other as well. Indeed when it comes to the losses of the Ratkin, the Bastet probably killed far more of them than the Garou simply because during the time period of the War of Rage, rats were still mainly limited to Southeast Asia where there weren't wolves, but plenty of big cats.<br /> <br /> So in my mind, there are probably very long term processes that lead to the losses and extinction of the other Changing Breeds. The Garou had a role of course, but so did the other Changing Breeds since they were all competitors for human breeding stock and caerns. There were also conflicts because of belief of Wyrm taint. But there were also plenty of other factors. The Garou simply outcompeted their rivals over a time period of thousands of years.<br /> <br /> So why do the Garou get the blame? It's probably because when Galliards first started looking at this time period and created the concept of the War of Rage, they created some kind of narrative epic that turned a bunch of separate conflicts over thousands of years into a single &quot;War of Rage&quot; and claimed credit for it because at that time, it was a good idea since it made the Garou seem really badass and powerful. Then millennia later as values changed and the Children of Gaia really built up the guilt, it instead made the Garou look like heels and they became embarrassed and ashamed. The other Changing Breeds adopted the Garou narrative because it was a simple explanation that assigned blame to a single group who were claiming credit for it anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T14:23:35-07:00","id":1136371,"title":"","content":"Let's look at the results of the War of Rage:<br /> <br /> EXTINCTION<br /> Apis<br /> Camazotz (remnant surviving in the New World until later destroyed)<br /> Grondr<br /> Bastet - Qualmi (Eurasian branch only - actually extirpated, not extinct)<br /> <br /> NEAR-EXTINCTION<br /> Bastet-Ceilican<br /> Gurahl<br /> Ratkin<br /> Nagah<br /> Mokole<br /> <br /> SOME LOSSES<br /> Ananasi<br /> Bastet - Bagheera, Khan, Simba, Swara, Bubasti<br /> <br /> LEFT ALONE<br /> Corax<br /> Rokea<br /> <br /> NOT INVOLVED (NORTH AMERICA)<br /> Nuwisha<br /> Bastet - Balam, Pumonca, Qualmi (North American branch)<br /> <br /> I see some general patterns. First, the breeds that became extinct were those that aren't really predators (I'll also include the Ratkin here). Such species are going to be at a disadvantage going up against outright predator species in competition for resources. Second, two of the breeds who suffered heavy losses are the only reptilian breeds. They stick out like sore thumbs in an environment of non-reptiles, and since they have less in common have a harder time finding common ground and more easily used as scapegoats.<br /> <br /> It's only the last group of breeds who suffered heavy losses that may require more explanation. Those include the Gurahl and two of the Bastet, the Ceilican and Eurasian Qualmi. The Ceilican are based on the very small wildcats. Not surprising they lost out here. The Eurasian Lynx is more surprising. It is smaller than the wolf, but not by much. However. it's range overlaps with that of the wolf. It may simply be a case of local Garou extirpating local Eurasian Qualmi in all these contested areas until over a long enough time the last hold outs die. Or more heretically, perhaps the Eurasian Qualmi never existed at all (there seems to be no actual stories about the Eurasian lynxes, just comments that there aren't any).<br /> <br /> That leaves just the Gurahl, and here we have one of the few concrete stories of an actual war with a real reason - the Gurahl refusal to teach the Garou the gift that brings the dead back to life. Although even here there are multiple reasons given for the Garou battling the Gurahl some of which predate even the Impergium. Nevertheless, we do have the idea here that there was an actual concerted effort to kill the Gurahl.<br /> <br /> All the other breeds seem to get off fairly lightly. Not surprising since they all live in lands where wolves are mostly absent, or possess traits which make them non-competitors to Garou or can easily get away from them (Corax can fly and complement wolves (in ways that bats do not), Rokea don't even live on the land, and the Ananasi can easily hide).<br /> <br /> In terms of the more successful &quot;peace&quot; in North America, we have far fewer Changing Breeds because the Americas lacked many of the animal species. Nuwisha are practically Garou anyway, and coyotes avoid wolves. Balam live in areas where there are not wolves. So it is just really the Pumonca and Qualmi who emerge as possible competitors, and unlike the very small Celican, they are much bigger with lynxes smaller, but cougars bigger than wolves.<br /> <br /> But two interesting things emerge. One there aren't any noticeably more Mokole or Nagah in the Americas despite there not being a War of Rage there. Nor are there a whole lot more Gurahl. So despite there not being any such war, the demographics seem to be roughly the same. Hmm, isn't that interesting? That tells me there was just as much competition and killing in North America as there was in Eurasia. There's just two major differences. Unlike in Eurasia, the Three Brothers never had a directed actual conflict against the Gurahl like the Silver Fangs lead over the gift to bring back the dead. The other is that the Pure Ones never developed a historical narrative of a war against the Changing Breeds in their history even though they basically fought and killed the other Changing Breeds at the same rate as the Eurasian tribes. The only reason why the Old World has a War of Rage and the New World does not is simply because each group's historians picked different narratives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 09-07-2017, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T16:49:14-07:00","id":1136437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134864-how-were-garou-able-to-hunt-down-other-feras-to-near-extinction?p=1136371#post1136371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's look at the results of the War of Rage:<br /> <br /> EXTINCTION<br /> <br /> <br /> But two interesting things emerge. One there aren't any noticeably more Mokole or Nagah in the Americas despite there not being a War of Rage there. Nor are there a whole lot more Gurahl. So despite there not being any such war, the demographics seem to be roughly the same. Hmm, isn't that interesting? That tells me there was just as much competition and killing in North America as there was in Eurasia. There's just two major differences. Unlike in Eurasia, the Three Brothers never had a directed actual conflict against the Gurahl like the Silver Fangs lead over the gift to bring back the dead. The other is that the Pure Ones never developed a historical narrative of a war against the Changing Breeds in their history even though they basically fought and killed the other Changing Breeds at the same rate as the Eurasian tribes. The only reason why the Old World has a War of Rage and the New World does not is simply because each group's historians picked different narratives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't there a notable amount of Mokole in the New world? They may not be a separate stream from Africa so I guess one could argue their numbers are depressed vs India, SE Asia and Australia where they have a different stream but they seem to have a sizable number among American crocadilians and even Gilamonsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}